{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000041-0","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"pelican\\n\",\"new_string\":\"pelican\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"Wrote file successfully to <home>/staff/gail/notes/live.md.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"Wrote file successfully to <home>/staff/gail/notes/live.md.\",\"absolute_path\":\"<home>/staff/gail/notes/live.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"pelican\\n\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"pelican\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000041-1","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchTool\",\"result_count\":5,\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"results\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"server\\\": \\\"office\\\",\\n      \\\"tools\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"office__my_access\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Your level, and each outside tool the owner gave you: what it reaches, or why a run leaves it out for now.\\\",\\n          \\\"score\\\": 4.739017963409424,\\n          \\\"input_schema\\\": {\\n            \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\\\",\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n            \\\"properties\\\": {}\\n          }\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"office__ask_for_access\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Ask the owner to connect a tool for you. Pass a catalog id or registry name from find_connectors, or the https address of a hosted MCP server. Ask for the lowest level that does the job: read to look, write to change things in the tool (needs act permission). If they approve, they get numbered steps to connect it, and it shows up in my_access when done.\\\",\\n          \\\"score\\\": 3.302743434906006,\\n          \\\"input_schema\\\": {\\n            \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\\\",\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n            \\\"properties\\\": {\\n              \\\"connector\\\": {\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n              },\\n              \\\"level\\\": {\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                \\\"enum\\\": [\\n                  \\\"read\\\",\\n                  \\\"write\\\"\\n                ],\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"read to look, write to change things in the tool.\\\"\\n              },\\n              \\\"why\\\": {\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"What job this access is for, in one or two sentences.\\\"\\n              },\\n              \\\"revises\\\": {\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"When the owner sent an ask back to rework, its id. Leave out otherwise.\\\",\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n                \\\"minimum\\\": -9007199254740991,\\n                \\\"maximum\\\": 9007199254740991\\n              }\\n            },\\n            \\\"required\\\": [\\n              \\\"connector\\\",\\n              \\\"level\\\",\\n              \\\"why\\\"\\n            ]\\n          }\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"office__reconnect_access\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"A tool the owner already gave you stopped working: its tools fail to load, or it turns down its key or sign-in. This puts the office's own steps to connect it again on the owner's desk, with a box for the new key and a Connect button, and no ask, since they said yes once. Never write those steps yourself with give_owner_a_task. Pass get_key only when the tool takes a key: how to get a new one, one action per step, naming the exact page and button.\\\",\\n          \\\"score\\\": 1.4253052473068237,\\n          \\\"input_schema\\\": {\\n            \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\\\",\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n            \\\"properties\\\": {\\n              \\\"connector\\\": {\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"The id my_access lists.\\\"\\n              },\\n              \\\"problem\\\": {\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                \\\"maxLength\\\": 300,\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"What went wrong and since when, in one or two sentences, with the error.\\\"\\n              },\\n              \\\"get_key\\\": {\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"How to get a new key, e.g. [\\\\\\\"Open https://console.apify.com/settings/integrations.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Copy your Personal API token. It starts with apify_api_.\\\\\\\"]\\\",\\n                \\\"maxItems\\\": 4,\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n                \\\"items\\\": {\\n                  \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                  \\\"maxLength\\\": 200\\n                }\\n              }\\n            },\\n            \\\"required\\\": [\\n              \\\"connector\\\",\\n              \\\"problem\\\"\\n            ]\\n          }\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"office__raise_ask\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Ask the owner to approve something. It lands on their desk and they approve, deny, or send it back with what to change, maybe with a reason. Use it for anything that needs their yes. One decision per ask, worded as the exact action: if they approve, you carry it out at once in a new run, with only the ask to go on. The reply lists their closest past decisions: if one matches and gave no reason, tell the owner that a reason would let Odds handle these without asking next time. For tool access use ask_for_access, and for a new Odd use propose_hire.\\\",\\n          \\\"score\\\": 1.2940454483032227,\\n          \\\"input_schema\\\": {\\n            \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\\\",\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n            \\\"properties\\\": {\\n              \\\"title\\\": {\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                \\\"maxLength\\\": 140,\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"What you want, as one short line: \\\\\\\"Unsubscribe you from the airline sale emails\\\\\\\".\\\"\\n              },\\n              \\\"why\\\": {\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"Why, in one to three plain sentences.\\\"\\n              },\\n              \\\"if_approved\\\": {\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"What happens next if they say yes.\\\"\\n              },\\n              \\\"attach\\\": {\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"Files in your folder that go with it, e.g. ['notes/intake.md']. the owner sees them on their desk and edits a Markdown one right there, so do not tell them where to find it.\\\",\\n                \\\"maxItems\\\": 5,\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n                \\\"items\\\": {\\n                  \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n                }\\n              },\\n              \\\"revises\\\": {\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"When the owner sent an ask back to rework, its id. Leave out otherwise.\\\",\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n                \\\"minimum\\\": -9007199254740991,\\n                \\\"maximum\\\": 9007199254740991\\n              }\\n            },\\n            \\\"required\\\": [\\n              \\\"title\\\",\\n              \\\"why\\\",\\n              \\\"if_approved\\\"\\n            ]\\n          }\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"tool_name\\\": \\\"office__hand_off\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Hand a colleague a piece of work their job covers. They start on it at once, in a run of their own, and when they finish, you pick up in a fresh run with their result. Do not wait for it: finish this run.\\\\n\\\\nA hand-off opens a thread you lead: each time work comes back you pick the next step in a fresh run, and you may hand on again in it, set a time to pick it back up, or ask the owner. Those runs see the thread, not this conversation, so put what the owner asked for in request, with every later step and condition. For more of the same work as a thread you lead, even a finished one, set continue_thread instead: it keeps that thread's folder, files and history, and a finished one reopens for a new round of work.\\\\n\\\\nA round of work starts with your estimate: in expect, how many hand-offs you expect it to take, and in expect_why, why, in plain words the owner may read on their desk, with no count of steps or hand-offs. It is your limit for that round. Over 20, the office asks the owner before the work starts. Past the limit the office refuses the hand-off, and you may ask for more the same way: hand_off again with expect set to how many more you need, and expect_why the same way; the owner answers, and the thread waits until then.\\\\n\\\\nWrite the brief for them: what to do, why, and what to send back. Give them everything they need and nothing more: pass on details about the owner's family, or anything from a goal they do not serve, only when their job covers it.\\\\n\\\\nIn shares_from, name each tool whose contents the work carries, in the brief or in the thread's folder: the ids my_access lists, or [] for none. On a thread, that includes a tool of a colleague's on it whose contents its part of the folder carries. Never copy anything from a tool the colleague lacks (the list below says which of yours) into the brief or the folder without naming it there. When you name one they lack, the hand-off waits on the owner's yes, and a no brings you back.\\\\n\\\\nTheir run works at Draft at most and cannot hand on, so they can pre… [truncated]\\\",\\n          \\\"score\\\": 0.7549690008163452,\\n          \\\"input_schema\\\": {\\n            \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\\\",\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n            \\\"properties\\\": {\\n              \\\"to\\\": {\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"The colleague's id, from the list.\\\"\\n              },\\n              \\\"title\\\": {\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n                \\\"maxLength\\\": 120,\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"This piece of the work, in one line.\\\"\\n              },\\n              \\\"brief\\\": {\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n                \\\"maxLength\\\": 4000,\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"What to do, why, and what to send back, with full paths to any files.\\\"\\n              },\\n              \\\"shares_from\\\": {\\n                \\\"maxItems\\\": 20,\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n                \\\"items\\\": {\\n                  \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n                },\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"Ids of the tools, from my_access or a colleague's on the thread, whose contents this work carries in the brief or the thread's folder. [] for none.\\\"\\n              },\\n              \\\"request\\\": {\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"When this opens a thread: what the owner asked for, in full, with any later steps or conditions (a pause, who checks it). Your later runs on the thread see this. Defaults to title.\\\",\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n                \\\"maxLength\\\": 600\\n              },\\n              \\\"goal\\\": {\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"When this opens a thread: the id of a goal you serve that it is for, if any.\\\",\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n                \\\"minimum\\\": -9007199254740991,\\n                \\\"maximum\\\": 9007199254740991\\n              },\\n              \\\"expect\\\": {\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"When this opens a thread, continues a finished one, or is the first on a thread with no estimate: how many hand-offs you expect this round to take. Once you have used them all: how many more you need. Leave out otherwise.\\\",\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n                \\\"minimum\\\": 1,\\n                \\\"maximum\\\": 100\\n              },\\n              \\\"expect_why\\\": {\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"With expect: why, in one plain line the owner may read on their desk. No count of steps or hand-offs: \\\\\\\"each lesson needs a page, then a check\\\\\\\".\\\",\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n                \\\"minLength\\\": 1,\\n                \\\"maxLength\\\": 300\\n              },\\n              \\\"continue_thread\\\": {\\n                \\\"description\\\": \\\"The id of a thread you lead, from \\\\\\\"Threads you lead\\\\\\\" in your instructions, when this is more of its work. Leave out request and goal: it keeps its own. Leave this out for new work.\\\",\\n                \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n                \\\"minimum\\\": -9007199254740991,\\n                \\\"maximum\\\": 9007199254740991\\n              }\\n            },\\n            \\\"required\\\": [\\n              \\\"to\\\",\\n              \\\"title\\\",\\n              \\\"brief\\\",\\n              \\\"shares_from\\\"\\n            ]\\n          }\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"total_hidden_tools\\\": 19,\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\\n  \\\"note\\\": null\\n}\"}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001","uuid":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000051"}
